        "---\n",
        "title: \"Title Tag Normalization Review\"\n",
        "subtitle: \"Deterministic normalization with guarded RapidFuzz consolidation\"\n",
        "format:\n",
        "  html:\n",
        "    toc: true\n",
        "    code-fold: false\n",
        "    embed-resources: true\n",
        "jupyter: python3\n",
        "execute:\n",
        "  echo: true\n",
        "  warning: false\n",
        "params:\n",
        "  fuzzy_score_cutoff: 86\n",
        "  fuzzy_high_confidence_cutoff: 96\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## Purpose\n",
        "\n",
        "This notebook applies the selected starting workflow for turning free-form\n",
        "title tags into stable normalized labels. It does not update classification\n",
        "results or publish a normalization dictionary.\n",
        "\n",
        "The two stages are intentionally conservative:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. deterministic surface normalization;\n",
        "2. guarded RapidFuzz alias consolidation.\n",
        "\n",
        "Deterministic equivalences and guarded high-confidence RapidFuzz aliases are\n",
        "applied to a final canonical mapping. Numeric differences, compound tags, and\n",
        "broader families are left unchanged. Embeddings and BERTopic-style clustering\n",
        "are deferred until tags have descriptor types that prevent unrelated facets\n",
        "from being compared.\n",
        "\n",
        "The original tag remains the auditable source value. A future production layer\n",
        "should map it to a canonical tag and broader family rather than rewriting the\n",
        "stored model response.\n",
        "\n",
        "Render the offline deterministic and RapidFuzz baseline from the repository\n",
        "root:\n",
        "\n",
        "```bash\n",
        "QUARTO_PYTHON=.venv/bin/python quarto render \\\n",
        "  py_scripts/notebooks/model_tests/tag_normalization/tag_normalization_model_review.qmd\n",
        "```"
      ],
      "id": "7c7b8d29"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: setup\n",
        "\n",
        "from __future__ import annotations\n",
        "\n",
        "import itertools\n",
        "import json\n",
        "import os\n",
        "import re\n",
        "import unicodedata\n",
        "from collections import defaultdict\n",
        "from pathlib import Path\n",
        "\n",
        "import duckdb\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "from rapidfuzz import fuzz, process\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def find_repo_root(start: Path | None = None) -> Path:\n",
        "    current = (start or Path.cwd()).resolve()\n",
        "    for candidate in (current, *current.parents):\n",
        "        if (candidate / \".git\").exists():\n",
        "            return candidate\n",
        "    raise RuntimeError(f\"Could not find the repository root from {current}.\")\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "REPO_ROOT = find_repo_root()\n",
        "os.chdir(REPO_ROOT)\n",
        "\n",
        "from py_scripts.lib.utils.env import load_repo_env\n",
        "from py_scripts.lib.utils.paths import unified_database_path\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "load_repo_env(REPO_ROOT)\n",
        "PARAMS = globals().get(\"params\", {})\n",
        "FUZZY_SCORE_CUTOFF = float(PARAMS.get(\"fuzzy_score_cutoff\", 86))\n",
        "FUZZY_HIGH_CONFIDENCE_CUTOFF = max(\n",
        "    float(PARAMS.get(\"fuzzy_high_confidence_cutoff\", 96)),\n",
        "    FUZZY_SCORE_CUTOFF,\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "pd.set_option(\"display.max_colwidth\", 120)"
      ],
      "id": "setup",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Load the current active-version tags\n",
        "\n",
        "Only results matching the current title hash and active title version are used.\n",
        "This prevents old title versions from making the vocabulary appear more\n",
        "fragmented than the current production state."
      ],
      "id": "78580184"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: load-current-tags\n",
        "\n",
        "database_path = unified_database_path()\n",
        "connection = duckdb.connect(str(database_path), read_only=True)\n",
        "try:\n",
        "    result_rows = connection.execute(\n",
        "        \"\"\"\n",
        "        SELECT\n",
        "          result.video_id,\n",
        "          result.talent_code,\n",
        "          talent.talent_name,\n",
        "          video.title,\n",
        "          status.title_version_id,\n",
        "          result.classification_json,\n",
        "          result.created_at\n",
        "        FROM classification.title_classification_status AS status\n",
        "        JOIN classification.title_classification_results AS result\n",
        "          ON result.video_id = status.video_id\n",
        "         AND result.title_hash = status.title_hash\n",
        "         AND result.title_version_id = status.title_version_id\n",
        "        JOIN catalog.videos AS video\n",
        "          ON video.video_id = result.video_id\n",
        "        LEFT JOIN catalog.talents AS talent\n",
        "          ON talent.talent_code = result.talent_code\n",
        "        WHERE status.is_classified\n",
        "        QUALIFY ROW_NUMBER() OVER (\n",
        "          PARTITION BY result.video_id\n",
        "          ORDER BY result.created_at DESC NULLS LAST,\n",
        "                   result.confidence DESC NULLS LAST\n",
        "        ) = 1\n",
        "        ORDER BY result.video_id\n",
        "        \"\"\"\n",
        "    ).fetchdf()\n",
        "finally:\n",
        "    connection.close()\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def parse_classification(value: object) -> dict[str, object]:\n",
        "    if value is None or pd.isna(value):\n",
        "        return {}\n",
        "    try:\n",
        "        parsed = json.loads(str(value))\n",
        "    except (TypeError, ValueError, json.JSONDecodeError):\n",
        "        return {}\n",
        "    return parsed if isinstance(parsed, dict) else {}\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "tag_records: list[dict[str, object]] = []\n",
        "for row in result_rows.itertuples(index=False):\n",
        "    classification = parse_classification(row.classification_json)\n",
        "    tags = classification.get(\"tags\", [])\n",
        "    if not isinstance(tags, list):\n",
        "        continue\n",
        "    for tag in tags:\n",
        "        tag_text = str(tag).strip()\n",
        "        if not tag_text:\n",
        "            continue\n",
        "        tag_records.append(\n",
        "            {\n",
        "                \"video_id\": row.video_id,\n",
        "                \"talent_code\": row.talent_code,\n",
        "                \"talent_name\": row.talent_name,\n",
        "                \"title\": row.title,\n",
        "                \"title_version_id\": row.title_version_id,\n",
        "                \"topic\": str(classification.get(\"topic\", \"\") or \"\"),\n",
        "                \"primary_reference\": str(\n",
        "                    classification.get(\"primary_reference\", \"\") or \"\"\n",
        "                ),\n",
        "                \"raw_tag\": tag_text,\n",
        "            }\n",
        "        )\n",
        "\n",
        "tag_rows = pd.DataFrame(tag_records)\n",
        "raw_inventory = (\n",
        "    tag_rows.groupby(\"raw_tag\", as_index=False)\n",
        "    .agg(\n",
        "        uses=(\"video_id\", \"size\"),\n",
        "        unique_titles=(\"video_id\", \"nunique\"),\n",
        "        talents=(\"talent_code\", \"nunique\"),\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    .sort_values([\"uses\", \"raw_tag\"], ascending=[False, True])\n",
        "    .reset_index(drop=True)\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "pd.DataFrame(\n",
        "    {\n",
        "        \"metric\": [\n",
        "            \"Current classified titles\",\n",
        "            \"Tag assignments\",\n",
        "            \"Distinct raw tags\",\n",
        "        ],\n",
        "        \"value\": [len(result_rows), len(tag_rows), len(raw_inventory)],\n",
        "    }\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "id": "load-current-tags",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Stage 1: deterministic surface normalization\n",
        "\n",
        "This stage should resolve differences that do not require semantic judgment:\n",
        "case, Unicode width, underscores, hyphens, surrounding punctuation, compact\n",
        "spellings, and a small number of transparent token aliases.\n",
        "\n",
        "Numbers are preserved. `15k_sub_goal` and `20k_sub_goal` may share a broader\n",
        "family, but they are not interchangeable aliases."
      ],
      "id": "1baceebb"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: deterministic-normalization\n",
        "\n",
        "COMPACT_TOKEN_ALIASES = {\n",
        "    \"masterduel\": \"master duel\",\n",
        "    \"subgoal\": \"sub goal\",\n",
        "    \"yugioh\": \"yu gi oh\",\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def normalize_tag(value: object) -> str:\n",
        "    text = unicodedata.normalize(\"NFKC\", str(value)).casefold().strip()\n",
        "    text = text.replace(\"&\", \" and \")\n",
        "    text = re.sub(r\"[_/\\\\-]+\", \" \", text)\n",
        "    text = re.sub(r\"(?<=\\d)(?=[a-z])|(?<=[a-z])(?=\\d)\", \" \", text)\n",
        "    text = re.sub(r\"[^\\w\\s]\", \" \", text, flags=re.UNICODE)\n",
        "    text = re.sub(r\"\\s+\", \" \", text).strip()\n",
        "\n",
        "    tokens = text.split()\n",
        "    expanded: list[str] = []\n",
        "    for token in tokens:\n",
        "        expanded.extend(COMPACT_TOKEN_ALIASES.get(token, token).split())\n",
        "    tokens = [\"hour\" if token == \"hours\" else token for token in expanded]\n",
        "    return \" \".join(tokens)\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def numeric_signature(value: object) -> tuple[str, ...]:\n",
        "    normalized = normalize_tag(value)\n",
        "    return tuple(re.findall(r\"\\b\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)?\\s*k?\\b\", normalized))\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "normalized_inventory = raw_inventory.copy()\n",
        "normalized_inventory[\"normalized_tag\"] = normalized_inventory[\"raw_tag\"].map(\n",
        "    normalize_tag\n",
        ")\n",
        "tag_rows[\"normalized_tag\"] = tag_rows[\"raw_tag\"].map(normalize_tag)\n",
        "normalized_groups = (\n",
        "    tag_rows.groupby(\"normalized_tag\", as_index=False)\n",
        "    .agg(\n",
        "        raw_variants=(\"raw_tag\", lambda values: \" | \".join(sorted(set(values)))),\n",
        "        variant_count=(\"raw_tag\", \"nunique\"),\n",
        "        uses=(\"video_id\", \"size\"),\n",
        "        unique_titles=(\"video_id\", \"nunique\"),\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    .sort_values([\"variant_count\", \"uses\"], ascending=[False, False])\n",
        "    .reset_index(drop=True)\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "normalization_summary = pd.DataFrame(\n",
        "    {\n",
        "        \"metric\": [\n",
        "            \"Distinct raw tags\",\n",
        "            \"Distinct normalized tags\",\n",
        "            \"Labels removed by deterministic normalization\",\n",
        "            \"Normalized groups with multiple raw spellings\",\n",
        "        ],\n",
        "        \"value\": [\n",
        "            len(raw_inventory),\n",
        "            len(normalized_groups),\n",
        "            len(raw_inventory) - len(normalized_groups),\n",
        "            int((normalized_groups[\"variant_count\"] > 1).sum()),\n",
        "        ],\n",
        "    }\n",
        ")\n",
        "normalization_summary"
      ],
      "id": "deterministic-normalization",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: deterministic-review\n",
        "\n",
        "normalized_groups.loc[\n",
        "    normalized_groups[\"variant_count\"] > 1,\n",
        "    [\"normalized_tag\", \"raw_variants\", \"variant_count\", \"uses\"],\n",
        "].head(100)"
      ],
      "id": "deterministic-review",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
